    "offices": {
      "President": "Elected by popular vote with a running mate for deputy president; to win in the first round a candidate needs more than half of the votes nationally and at least a quarter of the votes in 24 of the 47 counties, otherwise the top two meet in a run-off. The president is head of state and of government, and the 2010 constitution limits presidents to two terms.",
      "National Assembly": "Its 349 members are 290 elected by first past the post in single-member constituencies, 47 women elected in the counties, and 12 nominated by the parties according to their seats; the Speaker is an ex officio member. It is the lower house of Parliament since the Senate was restored in 2013, and general elections are held on the second Tuesday of August every fifth year."
    }
